# ── Copyrighted material — NEVER commit ────────────────────────────
# Commercial ROMs supplied locally by the owner, and anything extracted
# from them. The build pipeline regenerates all of this on demand.
References/Roms/
*.nds
*.nds.log
*.gba
*.srm
*.sav
*.dsv

# Data extracted from ROMs (regenerate: python tools/build_gamedata.py)
# data/level_caps.json is a design table, not ROM art, and IS committed.
data/rom/
# data/maps/ is NOT ignored. CLAUDE.md "Hard rules" lists `data/maps/**`
# (hand-authored) in the Committed column, and the maps in there are drawn by
# hand in tools/build_maps.py -- no ROM is read to produce them, exactly like the
# committed tests/fixtures/maps/*.json. See data/maps/README.md for the rule that
# keeps it that way: ROM-EXTRACTED map geometry must never be written here.

# Assets extracted from ROMs (regenerate: python tools/extract_all.py)
assets/generated/
assets/sprites/
assets/tilesets/
assets/audio/
extracted/

# ROM-derived data + the Godot resources built on top of it.
# DATA_CONTRACT.md sections 6, 7 and 10. Regenerate: python tools/build_tilesets.py
data/rom/
data/tilesets/
resources/outdoor_sinnoh.tres
resources/outdoor_sinnoh.tres.uid

# ── Godot ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.godot/
.import/
export.cfg
export_presets.cfg
*.translation
android/
builds/

# ── Python tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
tools/.cache/
tools/_work/

# ── OS / editor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Pipeline backups (regenerated; never commit) ───────────────────
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
